   "pdf_hash": "05f3c8d3f0f2e89d",
   "pdf_lines": [
    "Page 1 of 4",
    "Quotation Request //",
    "US Government Publishing Office JACKET: 500-566",
    "Government Publishing and Print Procurement Quotations Due By:",
    "732 North Capitol Street, NW (Eastern Time)11:00 AM on 11/10/2026",
    "Washington DC 20401-",
    "Submit quotes online, unless otherwise instructed, via https://publish.gpo.gov/smallPurchase.",
    "Contractor must provide mandatory W-9 form before GPO makes payment.",
    "TITLE: 10x10 Branded Canopy Tent",
    "QUANTITY:5 SUBMISSION OF QUOTES: Vendor to submit quotes via GPO Publish",
    "(https://publish.gpo.gov/smallPurchase). Fax, email, and phone quotes are not acceptable. Late quotes will",
    "not be accepted. All problems submitting quotes via GPO Publish must be reported prior to bid opening",
    "time to 843.934.5516.",
    "***Contract Administrator for this job is Bruce Canzanella, bcanzanella@gpo.gov***",
    "TRIM SIZE: See Description",
    "SCHEDULE:",
    "Furnished Material will be available for pickup by 11/12/2026",
    "Deliver complete (to arrive at destination) by 12/30/2026",
    "F.O.B. destination",
    "QUALITY LEVEL: N Quality Assurance Through Attributes (GPO PUB 310.1, effective May 1979 (Rev.",
    "9-19)) applies.",
    "DESCRIPTION:",
    "Required Product: 10x10 Branded Canopy Tent",
    "General product Information:",
    "- Size: 10' x 10' (3.0 m x 3.0 m)",
    "- Shaded Area: 100 sq. ft. (9.0 sq. m)",
    "- Prints in white and Army Gold (PMS 123) on black background",
    "We require the North Carolina National Guard logo printed on all four (4) sides of the canopy",
    "peaks/valances, with the following text placed directly beneath the logo:",
    "-Front & Back Panels: NATIONALGUARD.COM/NC",
    "-Left & Right Panels: LIVE HERE. WORK HERE. SERVE HERE.",
    "- See attachments",
    "** 5 tents which include the following (Frames, Canopies, tent stakes, and rolling bags for transportation)",
    "and hexagonal, rust-proof legs.",
    "** Canopies should be waterproof, UV-protected and flame-resistant. Full - color dye sublimation",
    "** Contractor to adjust customer supplied files to fit their format. No modifications will be given for DTP",
    "services.",
    "Product Features:",
    "- Aluminum Frame: Lightweight Aircraft-Grade Aluminum",
    "- Top Fabric: Premium Duralon(R) PRO ? 600D",
    "- Polyester Fire Certifications: Meets CPAI-84, NFPA-701, & CAN/ULC-S109 Fire-Resistance",
    "GPO Contract Terms (GPO Pub. 310.2, effective December 1, 1987 (Rev. 1-18)) applies.",
    "Reports of Fraud, Waste, and Abuse can be made in strict confidence to the GPO Inspector General toll-free National Hotline 1-800-743-7574.",
    "JACKET:500566 DEPARTMENT OF THE ARMY 7-90566 BAC: 3711 19",
    "Your Contract Administrator is: Bruce Canzanella Call: (843) 934-5516 Written By: bcanzanella Reviewed By:",
    "Page 2 of 4",
    "Requirements.",
    "- Frame & Structural Features:DualCore(TM) Reinforced Frame: High durability for heavy usage.",
    "- Cross-Brace Ceiling Design: One-piece ceiling structure for overhead support and rigidity.",
    "- Leg Adjusters: Comfortable toggle-grip channels with 5 height options.",
    "- No-Pinch E-Z Lock & Release Corners: Pinch-free system for fast setup and take-down.",
    "- Welded Steel Foot Plate: Sturdy foundation for stable anchoring.",
    "- Impact Resistant Components: High-impact Nylon joints and anti-corrosion hardware.",
    "Dimensional & Weight Specifications (10' x 10'):",
    "- Steel Frame Shipping Weight 61 lbs.",
    "- Aluminum Frame Shipping Weight 52 lbs.",
    "- Top (Fabric) Shipping Weight 12 lbs.",
    "- Frame Box Dimensions 66\" L x 10\" W x 10\" H",
    "- Top Box Dimensions 27\" L x 15\" W x 4\" H",
    "- Folded Dimensions 62.5\" L x 8.5\" W x 8.5\" H",
    "- Maximum Peak Height 11' 2\"",
    "- Maximum Headroom 7' 1\"",
    "- Maximum Valance Clearance Height 6' 9\"",
    "Quantity: 5 - packaged in boxes of 1, 5 total boxes",
    "__________________________________________________________________",
    "BUY AMERICAN ACT - NOTE: In compliance with Contract Terms 310.2 (Rev. 01-18), Contractor must",
    "state within quote submitted either that the end product is a Domestic end product or a Foreign end product",
    "as defined in Contract Clause 37 for the requested promotional item. Domestic end product or Foreign end",
    "product must be indicated in the comments field when submitting Quotes using Contractor Connect. The",
    "contractor shall indicate \"product of unknown origin\" when it is unknown if the product offered is a",
    "domestic end product; in that instance, GPO will consider the [quote/bid] as a Foreign end product, in",
    "accordance with Contract Terms, Certifications C-2 (Buy American Certification), that components of",
    "unknown origin have been considered to have been mined, produced, or manufactured outside the United",
    "States.",
    "SUBCONTRACTING: The contractor may make contracts for the furnishing of all or any part of the",
    "supplies or work specified. Accordingly, Contract Clause 6, \"Subcontracts,\" of GPO Contract Terms (GPO",
    "Publication 310.2, effective December 1, 1987 (Rev. 6 01)), does not apply to this procurement.",
    "NOTE: Vendors are required to provide either a link to a website containing the item description and a",
